---
import ContentPage from '../components/ContentPage.astro';
---

<ContentPage
  title="Privacy — oh-my-md"
  description="Privacy information for the oh-my-md website and desktop app."
  lang="en"
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
  <h1>A local-first product and a static website</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    This website is static. It has no accounts, no website-owned telemetry, no document upload, and
    no advertising or analytics scripts.
  </p>
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>What the website does not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No account or sign-in is required.</li>
      <li>The website does not upload, store, or inspect your Markdown documents.</li>
      <li>There are no website-owned advertising, analytics, or telemetry scripts.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Normal network metadata</h2>
    <p>
      When you follow a download link, your browser and the hosting service may receive normal request
      metadata such as an IP address, time, user agent, and requested URL. Download assets currently
      live on GitHub, so GitHub’s own policies apply to those requests.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Desktop app updates</h2>
    <p>
      App update behavior is documented separately from this website. In particular, this first
      <strong>0.0.1</strong> release does not claim a working in-app updater. Do not treat this page as
      an update service.
    </p>
  </section>
</ContentPage>
